{"title":"Jay From You Bet! and His Hunter Cycles ‘Cross Bike – John Watson","link":"https://theradavist.com/you-bet-hunter-cycles-cross-bike","date":1789020642000,"content":"<p><em>While hanging out with Jay from <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/you-bet-and-neuhaus-metalworks-happy-hour\" target=\"_blank\">You Bet after the Made Bike Show</a>, John couldn’t resist documenting Jay’s latest build, a <a href=\"https://huntercycles.bigcartel.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter Cycles</a> ‘cross bike…</em><span></span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/747a566a734297d2737a5d677620ef2d4413bb4025352bc008c5aaaf748c97cb.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/163a96e101c9c5d0b5c0d65976a925d033a7433f00409f82050dc037144bbe29.jpg 640w, /media/747a566a734297d2737a5d677620ef2d4413bb4025352bc008c5aaaf748c97cb.jpg 1800w, /media/b638834f50646485f2b32d5e799e539a7a3c1906dbf78c4f380f2ea301d9a30f.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>There’s just something special about bikes of this era. My guess is this frame was built around 2010 or so. Early aughts for sure. Pre-“gravel”, when top tubes were flat, cantilevers were just fine, and 1 1/8″ headsets ruled supreme. The biggest 700c tubeless tire that fit most frames was the WTB Nano, around 40 mm wide.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f5cd25072eb1476ad64534c334da8fa9a790184b0c00ea313b75931e04ebc959.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/677da863e0a300769bd3320eb7396f5e8a4755d7d0e3af4a7afa9eec08fc961a.jpg 800w, /media/d0fce18219c13c8bf4084f7207eed046f209e3dff12d8405eef711ef434adf8c.jpg 1600w, /media/f5cd25072eb1476ad64534c334da8fa9a790184b0c00ea313b75931e04ebc959.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/aa3be9b646d0eac6a4df6e790a0cc5933c8ebca09b14c1bf680798cb0a6105a7.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/e6dc80a8876c08252023583f0cfc39bf9ec697ec4cb8758164226bb972145974.jpg 800w, /media/ca5af566581e7d2cfd8c2bed8e245db2e6a3bf07d6ccb6c5241b57f13451552e.jpg 1600w, /media/aa3be9b646d0eac6a4df6e790a0cc5933c8ebca09b14c1bf680798cb0a6105a7.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>They just don’t make ’em like they used to, and those of us who enjoyed underbiking singletrack and chunky doubletrack on them remember the sensations like it was yesterday. Holding on for dear life, pinned down a steep section of two-track, peeling down a mountain, rims screaming, hands throbbing. These were our “gravel bikes.” And ya know what? <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/2015-bruce-gordon-monster-cross\" target=\"_blank\">They’re still pretty dang good</a>.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/580e5b71f97c63763ae0a86c077ad9eaeb26169515048507e82abe21bd5385af.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ebb6c0a936c30c353fe0883acc107df166b1e9d67deae8d65f273876e43bc349.jpg 800w, /media/580e5b71f97c63763ae0a86c077ad9eaeb26169515048507e82abe21bd5385af.jpg 1600w, /media/d477bd299c24b1425be54ee0c35124c499c332b448a107dd3bf2ec39f28b1c9e.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/20bd5072d9f13f0034a16ebe25558e5cf44cdee7d798121ec8bd3d98311799a6.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/655049912a06bddf90a4bbecb08044c724fedf7b5d3a7ac0a9ea58424ef89e99.jpg 800w, /media/20bd5072d9f13f0034a16ebe25558e5cf44cdee7d798121ec8bd3d98311799a6.jpg 1600w, /media/f425d4862f27c20fb82fc004f2235777929e6d7e4bd3af02c6780d44092c87a8.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/000df1321ea538e68b664f38d0be41c9be61f265400d985336beb4768e647ea0.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/2d1fc0a5849ddbee7a7da145259204b4db05c75ceee8c32c704d3cc3bcd5f84f.jpg 800w, /media/000df1321ea538e68b664f38d0be41c9be61f265400d985336beb4768e647ea0.jpg 1600w, /media/ed6a7cc82ea8bef50918db14b1bd39d10d278b37d4d05df777c3e332d446d6f5.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Rick Hunter’s bikes of this era are iconic and are grail items. On the rear of the bike, his ability to form seat stays into elegant wishbones – while keeping the chainstays visually balanced – is uncanny. On the front of the bike, his version of the segmented fork – with an arched tube brazed under the crown – is equally iconic.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/d022b41384c6c419fb2a9daf2bf7cef8ffcfad29a6ebd6832d34bb782b449e0e.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/17e1bfe68a9b42f923e2d6f2d7546585ca34d4e8a48e8349dba8f44c2aa1881c.jpg 800w, /media/7783289a7577ad27c72abe0aa3cc7da2510a7662cd9ffc042ec6e930c79e489f.jpg 1600w, /media/d022b41384c6c419fb2a9daf2bf7cef8ffcfad29a6ebd6832d34bb782b449e0e.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/18eb943c384cb0a9b784eace35726fba9c8caa6ad3545eca79fc7a4927a70909.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/145013ecd806b68cc10d02094a4eaf143f08f5ca7233dfeb3c7b28f1bf4f351c.jpg 800w, /media/ae0f0ff38457ebf1a9d9ec90309ef5f04190a017ffb92530cbe838f6890e3915.jpg 1600w, /media/18eb943c384cb0a9b784eace35726fba9c8caa6ad3545eca79fc7a4927a70909.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Jay acquired this frame off of Facebook Marketplace before giving it a respray earlier this year. He’s had such a busy summer at the shop that he’s yet to even ride it, but I managed to document it fresh off the build stand.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/556f4e68145c717aa6505fccc991d4393cc13f450411328572a3bc7831d7b1a9.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/2f0b34b75d32e019afacd32376efdcbdad07868070dc994880d9472e0402294d.jpg 640w, /media/556f4e68145c717aa6505fccc991d4393cc13f450411328572a3bc7831d7b1a9.jpg 1800w, /media/75a671d6e71576cc87ce00a221f5967115388e7dc4cb60e252cfc867ea88b067.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>While Rick built these bikes for ‘cross racing, even if you don’t race between the ribbons, they make for great all-rounder bikes. Rick’s iconic bottle placement is designed for easy access while racing or just riding around. Jay filled the bosses with <a href=\"https://kingcage.com/\" target=\"_blank\">King Cages</a> and <a href=\"https://www.ponderosacyclery.com/onlineshop/ponderosa-cyclery-purist-water-bottle\" target=\"_blank\">Ponderosa Cyclery bottles</a>.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/ba1bd447a9b67efe66c0c0144edbf6007d3ddca1ab30bd06bbcf6b081dd2072f.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/b616ab68a57f3d70c24502e767013e5a093fcfca733614bab3d6a60488ec2206.jpg 800w, /media/ba1bd447a9b67efe66c0c0144edbf6007d3ddca1ab30bd06bbcf6b081dd2072f.jpg 1600w, /media/7e8b07c6b59d25abd48e04c9a9f07e6224c728981f03e566a66fd8add8f630d2.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/7ceb1a64b2ad2b74ea6a20b70fc7fe46ec051da6238c6ff85b2a0a67e617915c.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/2e2a212dc1c092405c47f19f89e409713248a5cfcb2e8576b06a252d5e7e8748.jpg 800w, /media/7ceb1a64b2ad2b74ea6a20b70fc7fe46ec051da6238c6ff85b2a0a67e617915c.jpg 1600w, /media/bbb74fffcfa5b163a4c37f0ab6ce5632dc6e53139f1f795673779dadb3548e5b.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/83b7ddf1549f61d84992d5639abe85ab6c52b22f19906371a9b7dc5e25491236.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/9df61e4d99e910d42148bbe769c4e3723c12ebd70e9a76e6868a27d174fb2694.jpg 800w, /media/83b7ddf1549f61d84992d5639abe85ab6c52b22f19906371a9b7dc5e25491236.jpg 1600w, /media/fe8a7304e7020d943175c51f928e71dc5088f8e8d2be122c6ed23e93ec45feb4.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>His parts kit is a reflection of how Jay likes to build not only his personal bikes but some of the bikes he’ll set up for sale within the You Bet inventory. A mix of US-made components with bomber, mostly cable-actuated drivetrain bits. Tying in turquoise color pops throughout are vintage Chris King hubs with KCNC skewers and a blue Paul Boxcar faceplate and top cap. HED Belgium plus rims are set up tubeless with <a href=\"https://www.sim.works/products/simworks-x-tomii-cycles-faraway\" target=\"_blank\">SimWorks </a><a href=\"https://www.sim.works/products/simworks-x-tomii-cycles-faraway\" target=\"_blank\">Tomii</a><a href=\"https://www.sim.works/products/simworks-x-tomii-cycles-faraway\" target=\"_blank\"> Faraway tires</a>.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/41b3bf11742caeaa1f67a063a25b4c13c1d9ddf6f4396c0c6718d34713284d72.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/2507eaaedb1a0468d0ef4f0a4ff26dc79ff5430772f61bcdeddf86d67534cc97.jpg 800w, /media/41b3bf11742caeaa1f67a063a25b4c13c1d9ddf6f4396c0c6718d34713284d72.jpg 1600w, /media/280e797a69e9f80994d42b499a44a00ccc733dd8f3c8216f34ec6f0e4253cf75.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/7fcb5e4da2fbac2ebf59eda94a66f4134bab46ec04cc8b7916df45798d28d021.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/4173333503c2971426f0bd2a681eafbcd5f33d40662428d20cc9d39c5eff58d7.jpg 800w, /media/7fcb5e4da2fbac2ebf59eda94a66f4134bab46ec04cc8b7916df45798d28d021.jpg 1600w, /media/fb434e5670ab068984995d6e2bf37a8dd4925cbab765fdb7550a67a01e14b26b.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/08c79842aaef2571104841ae1e9d4d7e9ac1bdaa2e4820b070c708bcb0311d28.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/d3ccfafa62aa2e6f94c31723df1cc73469d1665f34cc80ce6ecbcdc5ac14e3a9.jpg 800w, /media/08c79842aaef2571104841ae1e9d4d7e9ac1bdaa2e4820b070c708bcb0311d28.jpg 1600w, /media/1ea984cb74f9d0d4588aeeaa73ea6908d60d8c1fc6b6ada55f1d93d85b3991b2.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>For brakes, <a href=\"https://www.paulcomp.com/shop/components/brakes/cantilever-brakes/touring-cantilever/\" target=\"_blank\">Paul Component Touring Canti</a> on the rear and <a href=\"https://www.paulcomp.com/shop/components/brakes/cantilever-brakes/neo-retro/\" target=\"_blank\">Neo Retro</a> for more stopping power on the front, and <a href=\"https://www.paulcomp.com/shop/components/drivetrain/cranksets/100-percent-pure-paul-cranks/\" target=\"_blank\">Paul 100% Pure Cranks</a>. The build spec continues with a Thomson post<span>, one of those unicorn Kangaroo leather Specialized saddles – a gift from Josh Scriven –  <a href=\"https://www.sim.works/products/wonderer-bar\" target=\"_blank\">Sim Works Wonderer bars</a>, and Campagnolo Record 10-speed shifters mated to an XT mech that shifts</span> smoothly thanks to the J-Tec Shift Mate. Jay wanted a derailleur with a clutch and this worked out perfectly.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/00aaca2063190f6e6622c6578c805285c93e09a91356f69ec7f5df5620497b67.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/1f475ed32904f23d7073619fba508059b7bf60e2eb58ae3a6b2103d346eb6e5a.jpg 640w, /media/00aaca2063190f6e6622c6578c805285c93e09a91356f69ec7f5df5620497b67.jpg 1800w, /media/7c71c3df2390690dac30a60b910992c2d322de483ad791b33d91d8f1c6b9041c.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Nicely done, Jay! That’s a looker. It was so good to see ya, buddy, and as always, thanks for letting me document your builds.</p>\n<p>Check out You Bet on <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/_you.bet_/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">Instagram</a> and in person at:</p>\n<p>556 Searls Ave, Nevada City, CA 95959</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/you-bet-hunter-cycles-cross-bike\">Jay From You Bet! and His Hunter Cycles ‘Cross Bike</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cms.theradavist.com/\">The Radavist</a>.</p>","author":"John Watson","comments":"https://theradavist.com/you-bet-hunter-cycles-cross-bike#comments","siteTitle":"The Radavist","siteHash":"96eb481d8084f04a4602bac57874ba717baf56b758f45547b5caf2312da766ef","entryHash":"c33d951398d9ad420bd3ddfe38d746c4cc6e3bb41ce2878925671331f0da0c1e","category":"Cycling"}